      "evidence": "The mistaken operation is now explicitly the strictly next integer, floor(v)+1, not ordinary ceiling. For every fractional residue v in [0,1), including v=0, that operation returns 1, so it generates the entire universal false claim. The actual floor-zero boundary is correctly refuted.",
      "refutation_verdict": "pass",
      "original_issue": "C5EX-KEY-q712-nesting-C-CEILING-ZERO-BOUNDARY-RECOVERY3",
      "disposition": "REPAIRED_IN_RECOVERY4_PRIOR_FAILURE_PRESERVED"
